  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "After the reported 1948 crash of a craft at Aztec, New Mexico, there were said to be two sets of photos, and the ones the government took did not last and faded to blank. Scott Ramsey, a researcher of the Aztec case, tells Michels this, going back to the original story told by a writer named Frank Scully. If true, the official record of the crash would have been lost on purpose or by some strange property of the scene."
